se_content': '```markdown\n[STEP GOAL]: Load the data, parse the duration from dates_active column, and calculate the median damage to split storms into high and low damage groups.\n```\n```markdown\n# Data Loading and Initial Exploration\nI need to:\n1. Load the CSV file\n2. Parse the `dates_active` column to calculate storm duration\n3. Calculate median damage to split into high/low damage groups\n4. Prepare data for correlation analysis\n```\n```python\nimport pandas as pd\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy import stats\n\n# Load the data\ndf = pd.read_csv(\'./input/cost_data_with_errors.csv\')\n\n# Display basic info\nprint(f"Dataset shape: {df.shape}")\nprint(f"\\nColumns: {df.columns.tolist()}")\nprint(f"\\nFirst few rows:")\nprint(df.head())\n```\n```markdown\n# Duration Calculation\nThe `dates_active` column contains date ranges like "April 19 – 21". I need to parse these to calculate the duration of each storm\'s activity.\n```\n```python\n# Function to calculate duration from dates_active\ndef calculate_duration(date_str):\n    """Calculate duration in days from date range string."""\n    if pd.isna(date_str):\n        return np.nan\n    \n    # Handle various date formats\n    try:\n        # Split by common separators\n        parts = str(date_str).split(\'–\')  # en-dash\n        if len(parts) == 2:\n            start_str, end_str = parts[0].strip(), parts[1].strip()\n            # Extract day numbers\n            start_day = int(\'\'.join(filter(str.isdigit, start_str)))\n            end_day = int(\'\'.join(filter(str.isdigit, end_str)))\n            duration = end_day - start_day + 1\n            return duration\n        else:\n            return np.nan\n    except:\n        return np.nan\n\n# Apply duration calculation\ndf[\'duration\'] = df[\'dates_active\'].apply(calculate_duration)\n\n# Check for any NaN values in duration\nprint(f"Duration column - NaN count: {df[\'duration\'].isna().sum()}")\nprint(f"Duration column - Sample values: {df[\'duration\'].head(10).tolist()}")\n```\n```markdown\n# Median Damage Calculation\nNow I\'ll calculate the median damage and split the data into high and low damage groups.\n```\n```python\n# Calculate median damage\nmedian_damage = df[\'damage_USD\'].median()\nprint(f"Median damage: ${median_damage:,.2f}")\n\n# Split into high and low damage groups\ndf[\'damage_group\'] = df[\'damage_USD\'].apply(lambda x: \'high\' if x > median_damage else \'low\')\n\n# Check group distribution\nprint(f"\\nGroup distribution:")\nprint(df[\'damage_group\'].value_counts())\n\n# Check for NaN in damage_USD\nprint(f"\\ndamage_USD NaN count: {df[\'damage_USD\'].isna().sum()}")\n```\n```markdown\n# Data Preparation for Correlation\nNow I\'ll prepare the data for correlation analysis, ensuring we have valid values for both max_storm_cat and duration.\n```\n```python\n# Filter rows with valid data for correlation\ndf_valid = df.dropna(subset=[\'max_storm_cat\', \'duration\', \'damage_USD\'])\n\nprint(f"Valid data shape: {df_valid.shape}")\nprint(f"\\nMax storm category range: {df_valid[\'max_storm_cat\'].min()} - {df_valid[\'max_storm_cat\'].max()}")\nprint(f"Duration range: {df_valid[\'duration\'].min()} - {df_valid[\'duration\'].max()}")\n\n# Split into high and low damage groups\nhigh_damage = df_valid[df_valid[\'damage_group\'] == \'high\']\nlow_damage = df_valid[df_valid[\'damage_group\'] == \'low\']\n\nprint(f"\\nHigh damage group size: {len(high_damage)}")\nprint(f"Low damage group size: {len(low_damage)}")\n```\nTime consumed: 0.42s\nCode output:\nExit Code: 0\nOutput: \nDataset shape: (818, 11)\n\nColumns: [\'Unnamed: 0\', \'name\', \'dates_active\', \'max_storm_cat\', \'max_sust_wind\', \'min_p\', \'areas_affected\', \'damage_USD\', \'deaths\', \'year\', \'damage_imputed\']\n\nFirst few rows:\n   Unnamed: 0    name   dates_active  max_storm_cat  max_sust_wind   min_p  \\\n0           0  ARLENE  April\xa019\xa0– 21              1       43.44880   990.0   \n1           1    BRET   June\xa019