re present in the dataset.\n```\n```python\n# Required columns for STEM feature engineering\nrequired_columns = [\'Year\', \'Computer Science\', \'Engineering\', \'Math and Statistics\', \'Physical Sciences\']\n\n# Check which columns are present\nmissing_columns = [col for col in required_columns if col not in df.columns]\npresent_columns = [col for col in required_columns if col in df.columns]\n\nprint("Required columns:", required_columns)\nprint("Present columns:", present_columns)\nprint("Missing columns:", missing_columns)\n\n# Display data types of required columns\nprint("\\nData types of required columns:")\nprint(df[required_columns].dtypes)\n```\n```markdown\n# Step 3: Create STEM Feature and Calculate Statistics\n\nNow I\'ll create the STEM feature and calculate the mean and range for years 2000 and beyond.\n```\n```python\n# Create STEM feature: sum of Computer Science, Engineering, Math and Statistics, and Physical Sciences\ndf[\'STEM\'] = df[\'Computer Science\'] + df[\'Engineering\'] + df[\'Math and Statistics\'] + df[\'Physical Sciences\']\n\n# Filter for years 2000 and beyond (inclusive)\ndf_filtered = df[df[\'Year\'] >= 2000].copy()\n\n# Calculate statistics\nmean_STEM = df_filtered[\'STEM\'].mean()\nmax_STEM = df_filtered[\'STEM\'].max()\nmin_STEM = df_filtered[\'STEM\'].min()\nrange_STEM = max_STEM - min_STEM\n\n# Round to 2 decimal places\nmean_STEM_rounded = round(mean_STEM, 2)\nrange_STEM_rounded = round(range_STEM, 2)\n\n# Output final results\nprint(f"@mean_STEM[{mean_STEM_rounded}]")\nprint(f"@range_STEM[{range_STEM_rounded}]")\n```\nTime consumed: 0.01s\nCode output:\nExit Code: 0\nOutput: \nDataset shape: (42, 18)\n\nFirst 5 rows:\n   Year  Agriculture  Architecture  Art and Performance    Biology   Business  \\\n0  1970     4.229798     11.921005                 59.7  29.088363   9.064439   \n1  1971     5.452797     12.003106                 59.9  29.394403   9.503187   \n2  1972     7.420710     13.214594                 60.4  29.8102