ck": {\n    "question_id": 734,\n    "answers": {"answer_name": "computed_value"},\n    "format_targets": {"answer_name": "@answer_name[computed_value]"},\n    "evidence": {\n      "source_columns": [],\n      "sample_size": 0,\n      "method": "short method description",\n      "oracle_evidence": {"field_name": "value checked when semantic oracle asks for it"}\n    },\n    "verified": true,\n    "validator_report_id": null\n  }\n}\n```\nUse the exact answer names from the expected output format: For each continent:\n@continent_name[name]\n@correlation_coefficient[r_value]\n@p_value[p_value]\n@correlation_significance[significance]\nwhere "name" is the name of the continent.\nwhere "r_value" is a number between -1 and 1, rounded to two decimal places.\nwhere "p_value" is a number between 0 and 1, rounded to four decimal places.\nwhere "significance" is a string that can either be "significant" or "non-significant" based on the conditions specified in the constraints.\nIf a required field is unknown, continue verification instead of finalizing.\n\n# Branch Policy\nFollow the routed persistent rules deterministically. Emit hypothesis -> computation -> oracle check -> FinalAnswerBlock. Avoid alternative interpretations unless a validator or oracle check fails.\n\n```', 'response_content': '```markdown\n[STEP GOAL]: Load the gapminder dataset and perform Pearson correlation analysis between life expectancy (lifeexp) and GDP per capita (gdppercap) for each continent, including significance testing.\n```\n```markdown\nI need to:\n1. Load the gapminder_cleaned.csv file\n2. Verify the required columns exist (lifeexp, gdppercap, continent)\n3. Group data by continent\n4. Calculate Pearson correlation coefficient and p-value for each continent\n5. Determine significance based on the criteria (p < 0.05 AND |r| >= 0.5)\n6. Format the output as specified\n```\n```python\nimport pandas as pd\nfrom scipy.stats import pearsonr\n\n# Load the dataset\ndf = pd.read_csv(\'./input/gapminder_cleaned.csv\')\n\n# Display basic info\nprint("Dataset shape:", df.shape)\nprint("\\nColumn names:", df.columns.tolist())\nprint("\\nFirst few rows:")\nprint(df.head())\nprint("\\nContinents in dataset:")\nprint(df[\'continent\'].unique())\n```\n```python\n# Verify required columns exist\nrequired_columns = [\'lifeexp\', \'gdppercap\', \'continent\']\nmissing_cols = [col for col in required_columns if col not in df.columns]\nif missing_cols:\n    print(f"ERROR: Missing required columns: {missing_cols}")\nelse:\n    print("All required columns are present.")\n```\n```python\n# Perform correlation analysis for each continent\nresults = []\n\nfor continent in df[\'continent\'].unique():\n    # Filter data for this continent\n    continent_data = df[df[\'continent\'] == continent]\n    \n    # Get the values for life expectancy and GDP per capita\n    lifeexp = continent_data[\'lifeexp\'].dropna()\n    gdppercap = continent_data[\'gdppercap\'].dropna()\n    \n    # Find common indices\n    common_idx = lifeexp.index.intersection(gdppercap.index)\n    lifeexp_common = lifeexp.loc[common_idx]\n    gdppercap_common = gdppercap.loc[common_idx]\n    \n    # Calculate Pearson correlation and p-value\n    r, p_value = pearsonr(lifeexp_common, gdppercap_common)\n    \n    # Determine significance\n    # Significant if p < 0.05 AND |r| >= 0.5\n    if p_value < 0.05 and abs(r) >= 0.5:\n        significance = "significant"\n    else:\n        significance = "non-significant"\n    \n    # Store results\n    results.append({\n        \'continent\': continent,\n        \'r_value\': round(r, 2),\n        \'p_value\': round(p_value, 4),\n        \'significance\': significance,\n        \'sample_size\': len(common_idx)\n    })\n    \n    print(f"\\n{continent}:")\n    print(f"  Sample size: {len(common_idx)}")\n    print(f"  Correlation (r): {r:.4f}")\n    print(f"  P-value: {p_value:.4f}")\n    print(f"  Significance: {significance}")\n\n# Create results DataFrame\nresults_df = pd.DataFrame(results)\nprint("\\n\\nSummary of all continents:")\nprint(results_df)\n```\n```markdown\n[STEP GOAL]: <end_step>\n```\nTime consumed: 0.35s\nCode output:\nExit Code: 0\nOutput: \nDataset shape: (1704, 6)\n\nColumn names: [\'year\', \'pop\', \'lifeexp\', \'gdppercap\', \'country\', \'continent\']\n\nFirst few rows:\n   year       pop  lifeexp   gdppercap      country continent\n0  1952   8425333   28.801  779.445314  afghanistan      asia\n1  1957   9240934   30.332  820.853030  afghanistan      asia\n2  1962  10267083   31.997  853.100710  afghanistan      asia\n3  1967  11537966   34.020  836.197138  afghanistan      asia\n4  1972  13079460   36.088  739.981106  afghanistan      asia\n\nContinents in dataset:\n[\'asia\' \'europe\' \'africa\' \'americas\' \'oceania\']\n\nTime consumed: 0.00s\nCode output:\nExit Code: 0\nOutput: \nAll required columns are present.\n\nTime consumed: 0.01s\nCode output:\nExit Code: 0\nOutput: \n\nasia:\n  Sample size: 396\n  Correlation (r): 0.3820\n  P-value: 0.0000\n  Significance: non-significant\n\neurope:\n  Sample size: 360\n  Correlation (r): 0.7808\n  P-value: 0.0000\n  Significance: significant\n\nafrica:\n  Sample size: 624\n  Correlation (r): 0.4256\n  P-value: 0.0000\n  Significance: non-significant\n\namericas:\n  Sample size: 300\n  Correlation (r): 0.5584\n  P-value: 0.0000\n  Significance: significant\n\noceania:\n  Sample size: 24\n  Correlation (r): 0.9565\n  P-value: 0.0000\n  Significance: significant\n\n\nSummary of all continents:\n  continent  r_value  p_value     significance  sample_size\n0      asia     0.38      0.0  non-significant          396\n1    europe     0.78      0.0      significant          360\n2    africa     0.43      0.0  non-significant          624\n3  americas     0.56      0.0      significant          300\n4   oceania     0.96      0.0      significant           24\n\n```markdown\n[STEP GOAL]: Format the results according to the expected output format and create the FinalAnswer