r with p-value significance test"\n      }\n    },\n    "verified": true,\n    "validator_report_id": null\n  }\n}\n\n```markdown\n[STEP GOAL]: Format the results according to the expected output format and create the FinalAnswerBlock.\n\nThe correlation analysis has been completed successfully. Here\'s a summary of the results:\n\n| Continent | Correlation Coefficient (r) | P-value | Significance |\n|-----------|----------------------------|---------|--------------|\n| Asia | 0.38 | 0.0 | non-significant |\n| Europe | 0.78 | 0.0 | significant |\n| Africa | 0.43 | 0.0 | non-significant |\n| Americas | 0.56 | 0.0 | significant |\n| Oceania | 0.96 | 0.0 | significant |\n\nThe FinalAnswerBlock has been created with all required fields:\n- question_id: 734\n- answers: Contains all computed values for each continent\n- format_targets: Contains the @answer_name[value] formatted strings\n- evidence: Includes source_columns, sample_size, method, and oracle_evidence\n- verified: true\n\nAll correlation analyses were performed using Pearson correlation with a two-tailed test (alpha=0.05). Significance was determined based on the criteria: p < 0.05 AND |r| >= 0.5.\n```\n```markdown\n<end_step>\n```\n```markdown\n# Correlation Analysis Results: Life Expectancy vs GDP per Capita by Continent\n\n## Summary\nI have successfully performed Pearson correlation analysis between life expectancy (lifeexp) and GDP per capita (gdppercap) for each continent in the gapminder dataset. The analysis was conducted separately for each of the 5 continents.\n\n## Methodology\n- **Statistical Method**: Pearson correlation coefficient (r)\n- **Significance Test**: Two-tailed test with alpha = 0.05\n- **Significance Criteria**: \n  - Significant: p-value < 0.05 AND |r| >= 0.5\n  - Non-significant: p-value >= 0.05 OR |r| < 0.5\n\n## Results by Continent\n\n### Asia\n- **Correlation Coefficient (r)**: 0.38\n- **P-value**: 0.0000\n- **Significance**: non-significant\n- **Interpretation**: While the correlation is statistically significant (p < 0.05), the strength of the relationship (|r| = 0.38) is below the threshold of 0.5, making it non-significant by our criteria.\n\n### Europe\n- **Correlation Coefficient (r)**: 0.78\n- **P-value**: 0.0000\n- **Significance**: significant\n- **Interpretation**: Strong positive correlation between life expectancy and GDP per capita. Countries with higher GDP per capita tend to have higher life expectancy.\n\n### Africa\n- **Correlation Coefficient (r)**: 0.43\n- **P-value**: 0.0000\n- **Significance**: non-significant\n- **Interpretation**: Moderate correlation that is statistically significant but below the 0.5 threshold for practical significance.\n\n### Americas\n- **Correlation Coefficient (r)**: 0.56\n- **P-value**: 0.0000\n- **Significance**: significant\n- **Interpretation**: Moderate to strong positive correlation. Higher GDP per capita is associated with higher life expectancy in this region.\n\n### Oceania\n- **Correlation Coefficient (r)**: 0.96\n- **P-value**: 0.0000\n- **Significance**: significant\n- **Interpretation**: Very strong positive correlation. This is the strongest relationship observed across all continents, indicating that GDP per capita is a very strong predictor of life expectancy in Oceania.\n\n## Key Findings\n1. **Strongest Correlation**: Oceania (r = 0.96) shows the strongest relationship between life expectancy and GDP per capita.\n2. **Weakest Correlation**: Asia (r = 0.38) shows the weakest relationship, though still positive.\n3. **Significant Correlations**: Europe, Americas, and Oceania show significant correlations (p < 0.05 AND |r| >= 0.5).\n4. **Non-Significant Correlations**: Asia and Africa show non-significant correlations due to |r| < 0.5, despite having p-values < 0.05.\n5. **Universal Positive Relationship**: All continents show positive correlations, indicating that higher GDP per capita is generally associated with higher life expectancy across all regions.\n\n## Data Quality\n- **Total Observations**: 1,704 country-year combinations\n- **Missing Values**: 0% (all required columns complete)\n- **Continents Analyzed**: 5 (Asia, Europe, Africa, Americas, Oceania)\n\n## Final Answer Block\n```\n```markdown\n{\n  "final_answer_block": {\n    "question_id": 734,\n    "answers": {\n      "continent_name_asia": "asia",\n      "correlation_coefficient_asia": 0.38,\n      "p_value_asia": 0.0,\n      "correlation_significance_asia": "non-significant",\n      "continent_name_europe": "europe",\n      "correlation_coefficient_europe": 0.78,\n      "p_value_europe": 0.0,\n      "correlation_significance_europe": "significant",\n      "continent_name_africa": "africa",\n      "correlation_coefficient_africa": 0.43,\n      "p_value_africa": 0.0,\n      "correlation_significance_africa": "non-significant",\n      "continent_name_americas": "americas",\n      "correlation_coefficient_americas": 0.56,\n      "p_value_americas": 0.0,\n      "correlation_significance_americas": "significant",\n      "continent_name_oceania": "oceania",\n      "correlation_coefficient_oceania": 0.96,\n      "p_value_oceania": 0.0,\n      "correlation_significance_oceania": "significant"\n    },\n    "format_targets": {\n      "continent_name_asia": "@continent_name[asia]",\n      "correlation_coefficient_asia": "@correlation_coefficient[0.38]",\n      "p_value_asia": "@p_value[0.0]",\n      "correlation_significance_asia": "@correlation_significance[non-significant]",\n      "continent_name_europe": "@continent_name[europe]",\n      "correlation_coefficient_europe": "@correlation_coefficient[0.78]",\n      "p_value_europe": "@p_value[0.0]",\n      "correlation_significance_europe": "@correlation_significance[significant]",\n      "continent_name_africa": "@continent_name[africa]",\n      "correlation_coefficient_africa": "@correlation_coefficient[0.43]",\n      "p_value_africa": "@p_value[0.0]",\n      "correlation_significance_africa": "@correlation_significance[non-significa