\n\n# Load the dataset\ndf = pd.read_csv(\'./input/gapminder_cleaned.csv\')\n\n# Display basic info about the dataset\nprint("Dataset shape:", df.shape)\nprint("\\nColumn names:", df.columns.tolist())\nprint("\\nContinents in dataset:", df[\'continent\'].unique())\nprint("\\nFirst few rows:")\nprint(df.head())\n```\n```python\n# Perform correlation analysis for each continent\nresults = []\n\nfor continent in df[\'continent\'].unique():\n    # Filter data for the current continent\n    continent_data = df[df[\'continent\'] == continent]\n    \n    # Calculate Pearson correlation coefficient and p-value\n    r, p_value = pearsonr(continent_data[\'lifeexp\'], continent_data[\'gdppercap\'])\n    \n    # Determine significance\n    # Significant if p-value < 0.05 AND |r| >= 0.5\n    if p_value < 0.05 and abs(r) >= 0.5:\n        significance = "significant"\n    else:\n        significance = "non-significant"\n    \n    # Store results\n    results.append({\n        \'continent\': continent,\n        \'r_value\': round(r, 2),\n        \'p_value\': round(p_value, 4),\n        \'significance\': significance,\n        \'sample_size\': len(continent_data)\n    })\n\n# Create results DataFrame\nresults_df = pd.DataFrame(results)\nprint("Correlation Analysis Results by Continent:")\nprint(results_df.to_string(index=False))\n```\n```markdown\n[STEP GOAL]: Format the results according to the expected output format and prepare the FinalAnswerBlock.\n```\n```python\n# Format the output according to the expected format\nformatted_output = []\n\nfor _, row in results_df.iterrows():\n    formatted_output.append(f"@continent_name[{row[\'continent\']}]")\n    formatted_output.append(f"@correlation_coefficient[{row[\'r_value\']}]")\n    formatted_output.append(f"@p_value[{row[\'p_value\']}]")\n    formatted_output.append(f"@correlation_significance[{row[\'significance\']}]")\n    formatted_output.append("")  # Empty line between continents\n\n# Print formatted output\nprint("Formatted Output:")\nprint("\\n".join(formatted_output))\n```\n```markdown\n[STEP GOAL]: Create the FinalAnswerBlock with all required fields and submit the final answer.\n```\n```python\nimport json\n\n# Prepare the answers dictionary\nanswers = {}\nformat_targets = {}\n\nfor _, row in results_df.iterrows():\n    answers[f"{row[\'continent\']}_correlation_coefficient"] = row[\'r_value\']\n    answers[f"{row[\'continent\']}_p_value"] = row[\'p_value\']\n    answers[f"{row[\'continent\']}_significance"] = row[\'significance\']\n    \n    format_targets[f"{row[\'continent\']}_correlation_coefficient"] = f"@correlation_coefficient[{row[\'r_value\']}]"\n    format_targets[f"{row[\'continent\']}_p_value"] = f"@p_value[{row[\'p_value\']}]"\n    format_targets[f"{row[\'continent\']}_significance"] = f"@correlation_significance[{row[\'significance\']}]"\n    format_targets[f"{row[\'continent\']}_continent_name"] = f"@continent_name[{row[\'continent\']}]"\n\n# Create the FinalAnswerBlock\nfinal_answer_block = {\n    "final_answer_block": {\n        "question_id": 734,\n        "answers": answers,\n        "format_targets": format_targets,\n        "evidence": {\n            "source_columns": ["lifeexp", "gdppercap", "continent"],\n            "sample_size": len(df),\n            "method": "Pearson correlation coefficient with two-tailed test (alpha=0.05)",\n            "oracle_evidence": {\n                "feature_columns": ["gdppercap"],\n                "target": "lifeexp",\n                "split": "grouped by continent",\n                "random_state": "N/A (correlation analysis)",\n                "metric": "Pearson r and p-value"\n            }\n        },\n        "verified": True,\n        "validator_report_id": None\n    }\n}\n\n# Print the FinalAnswerBlock\nprint(json.dumps(final_answer_block, indent=2))\n```\n```markdown\n# Final Answer\n\nBased on the correlation analysis between life expectancy and GDP per capita for each continent:\n```\n```markdown\n{\n  "final_answer_