um()\nbalance_missing = credit_df[\'Balance\'].isnull().sum()\nprint(f"Missing values in Income column: {income_missing}")\nprint(f"Missing values in Balance column: {balance_missing}")\n```\n```python\n# If there are missing values in Education, impute them with the mode\nif education_missing > 0:\n    credit_df[\'Education\'] = credit_df[\'Education\'].fillna(education_mode)\n    print(f"Imputed {education_missing} missing values in Education column with mode: {education_mode}")\nelse:\n    print("No missing values in Education column - no imputation needed")\n\n# Verify the Education column after imputation\nprint(f"\\nEducation column after imputation - Missing values: {credit_df[\'Education\'].isnull().sum()}")\n```\nTime consumed: 0.01s\nCode output:\nExit Code: 0\nOutput: \nDataFrame shape: (400, 12)\n\nColumn dtypes:\nUnnamed: 0      int64\nIncome        float64\nLimit           int64\nRating          int64\nCards           int64\nAge             int64\nEducation       int64\nGender         object\nStudent        object\nMarried        object\nEthnicity      object\nBalance         int64\ndtype: object\n\nTime consumed: 0.01s\nCode output:\nExit Code: 0\nOutput: \nMissing values in Education column: 0\nMode of Education column: 16\nMissing values in Income column: 0\nMissing values in Balance column: 0\n\nTime consumed: 0.00s\nCode output:\nExit Code: 0\nOutput: \nNo missing values in Education column - no imputation needed\n\nEducation column after imputation - Missing values: 0\n\n```markdown\n# Step 1 Complete: Data Loading and Missing Value Check\n\n## Results:\n- **DataFrame shape**: 400 rows × 12 columns\n- **Missing values in Education column**: 0\n- **Mode of Education column**: 16\n- **Missing values in Income column**: 0\n- **Missing values in Balance column**: 0\n\n## Conclusion:\nNo imputation is needed for the Education column as there are no missing values. The mode is 16, which will be reported in the final answer.\n\n---\n\n# Next Step Goal:\