ion is needed for Education column")\n    credit_df[\'Education\'] = credit_df[\'Education\'].fillna(education_mode)\nelse:\n    print("No imputation needed for Education column")\n```\n```markdown\nNow I need to perform Min-Max normalization on the "Income" and "Balance" columns. I\'ll calculate the min and max values, then apply the normalization formula.\n```\n```python\n# Get min and max values for Income column\nincome_min = credit_df[\'Income\'].min()\nincome_max = credit_df[\'Income\'].max()\nprint(f"Income - Min: {income_min}, Max: {income_max}")\n\n# Get min and max values for Balance column\nbalance_min = credit_df[\'Balance\'].min()\nbalance_max = credit_df[\'Balance\'].max()\nprint(f"Balance - Min: {balance_min}, Max: {balance_max}")\n\n# Apply Min-Max normalization to Income column\ncredit_df[\'Income_normalized\'] = (credit_df[\'Income\'] - income_min) / (income_max - income_min)\n\n# Apply Min-Max normalization to Balance column\ncredit_df[\'Balance_normalized\'] = (credit_df[\'Balance\'] - balance_min) / (balance_max - balance_min)\n\n# Display first few rows to verify normalization\nprint("\\nFirst 5 rows of normalized data:")\nprint(credit_df[[\'Income\', \'Income_normalized\', \'Balance\', \'Balance_normalized\']].head())\n```\n```markdown\nNow I need to save the normalized Income and Balance columns to separate CSV files and prepare the final output format.\n```\n```python\n# Save normalized Income to a CSV file\nincome_normalized_path = \'./working/income_normalized.csv\'\ncredit_df[[\'Income_normalized\']].to_csv(income_normalized_path, index=False)\n\n# Save normalized Balance to a CSV file\nbalance_normalized_path = \'./working/balance_normalized.csv\'\ncredit_df[[\'Balance_normalized\']].to_csv(balance_normalized_path, index=False)\n\n# Verify the files were created\nprint(f"Income normalized file path: {income_normalized_path}")\nprint(f"Balance normalized file path: {balance_normalized_path}")\n\n# Verify file contents\nprint("\\nIncome normalized file contents (first 5 rows):")\nprint(pd.read_csv(income_normalized_path).head())\n\nprint("\\nBalance normalized file contents (first 5 rows):")\nprint(pd.read_csv(balance_normalized_path).head())\n```\n```markdown\nNow I need to prepare the final output in the required format with rounded values.\n```\n```python\n# Round min and max values to 2 decimal places\nincome_min_rounded = round(income_min, 2)\nincome_max_rounded = round(income_max, 2)\nbalance_min_rounded = round(balance_min, 2)\nbalance_max_rounded = round(balance_max, 2)\n\n# Print final results\nprint("=" * 50)\nprint("FINAL RESULTS")\nprint("=" * 50)\nprint(f"education_mode: {education_mode}")\nprint(f"income_min_val: {income_min_rounded}")\nprint(f"income_max_val: {income_max_rounded}")\nprint(f"income_normalized_file_path: {income_normalized_path}")\nprint(f"balance_min_val: {balance_min_rounded}")\nprint(f"balance_max_val: {balance_max_rounded}")\nprint(f"balance_normalized_file_path: {balance_normalized_path}")\n```\n```markdown\n[STEP GOAL]: Create the FinalAnswerBlock with all computed values in the required format.\n```\n```markdown\nI will now create the FinalAnswerBlock with all the computed values in the exact format specified by the user.\n```\n```markdown\n{\n  "final_answer_block": {\n    "question_id": 743,\n    "answers": {\n      "education_mode": 11,\n      "income_normalization": [10.35, 186.63, "./working/income_normalized.csv"],\n      "balance_normalization": [0, 1999, "./working/balance_normalized.csv"]\n    },\n    "format_targets": {\n      "education_mode": "@education_mode[11]",\n      "income_normalization": "@income_normalization[10.35, 186.63, ./working/income_normalized.csv]",\n      "balance_normalization": "@balance_normalization[0, 1999, ./working/balance_normalized.csv]"\n    },\n    "evidence": {\n      "source_columns": ["Income", "Education", "Balance"],\n      "sample_size": 400,\n      "method": "Min-Max normalization and mode imputation",\n      "oracl