eck if there are any missing values that need imputation\nif education_missing > 0:\n    print(f"Imputing {education_missing} missing values with mode: {education_mode}")\n    credit_df[\'Education\'] = credit_df[\'Education\'].fillna(education_mode)\nelse:\n    print("No missing values to impute in \'Education\' column.")\n\n# Verify the Education column after imputation\nprint(f"\\nMissing values in \'Education\' after imputation: {credit_df[\'Education\'].isnull().sum()}")\n```\n```markdown\n# Step 3: Min-Max Normalization for Income and Balance\nNow I\'ll perform Min-Max normalization on the "Income" and "Balance" columns.\n```\n```python\n# Get min and max values for Income column\nincome_min = credit_df[\'Income\'].min()\nincome_max = credit_df[\'Income\'].max()\nprint(f"Income - Min: {income_min:.2f}, Max: {income_max:.2f}")\n\n# Get min and max values for Balance column\nbalance_min = credit_df[\'Balance\'].min()\nbalance_max = credit_df[\'Balance\'].max()\nprint(f"Balance - Min: {balance_min:.2f}, Max: {balance_max:.2f}")\n\n# Apply Min-Max normalization to Income column\ncredit_df[\'Income_normalized\'] = (credit_df[\'Income\'] - income_min) / (income_max - income_min)\n\n# Apply Min-Max normalization to Balance column\ncredit_df[\'Balance_normalized\'] = (credit_df[\'Balance\'] - balance_min) / (balance_max - balance_min)\n\n# Verify normalization (values should be between 0 and 1)\nprint(f"\\nIncome_normalized range: [{credit_df[\'Income_normalized\'].min():.4f}, {credit_df[\'Income_normalized\'].max():.4f}]")\nprint(f"Balance_normalized range: [{credit_df[\'Balance_normalized\'].min():.4f}, {credit_df[\'Balance_normalized\'].max():.4f}]")\n```\n```markdown\n# Step 4: Save Normalized Data to Files\nI\'ll save the normalized Income and Balance columns to separate CSV files.\n```\n```python\n# Define file paths for normalized data\nincome_normalized_path = \'./working/income_normalized.csv\'\nbalance_normalized_path = \'./working/balance_normalized.csv\'\n\n# Save normalized Income column\nincome_normalized_df = credit_df[[\'Income_normalized\']].copy()\nincome_normalized_df.to_csv(income_normalized_path, index=False)\nprint(f"Income normalized data saved to: {income_normalized_path}")\n\n# Save normalized Balance column\nbalance_normalized_df = credit_df[[\'Balance_normalized\']].copy()\nbalance_normalized_df.to_csv(balance_normalized_path, index=False)\nprint(f"Balance normalized data saved to: {balance_normalized_path}")\n\n# Verify the files were created\nprint(f"\\nIncome normalized file exists: {os.path.exists(income_normalized_path)}")\nprint(f"Balance normalized file exists: {os.path.exists(balance_normalized_path)}")\n```\n```markdown\n# Step 5: Prepare Final Answer\nNow I\'ll compile all the required values for the final answer.\n```\n```python\n# Round min and max values to 2 decimal places\nincome_min_rounded = round(income_min, 2)\nincome_max_rounded = round(income_max, 2)\nbalance_min_rounded = round(balance_min, 2)\nbalance_max_rounded = round(balance_max, 2)\n\n# Print final values\nprint("=" * 50)\nprint("FINAL ANSWER VALUES")\nprint("=" * 50)\nprint(f"education_mode: {education_mode}")\nprint(f"income_min_val: {income_min_rounded}")\nprint(f"income_max_val: {income_max_rounded}")\nprint(f"income_normalized_file_path: {income_normalized_path}")\nprint(f"balance_min_val: {balance_min_rounded}")\nprint(f"balance_max_val: {balance_max_rounded}")\nprint(f"balance_normalized_file_path: {balance_normalized_path}")\n```\n```markdown\n[STEP GOAL]: Create the FinalAnswerBlock with all computed values in the required format.\n```\n```markdown\n# Final Answer Block\nHere is the final answer in the required JSON format:\n```\n```markdown\n{\n  "final_answer_block": {\n    "question_id": 743,\n    "answers": {\n      "education_mode": 11,\n      "income_normalization": [10.35, 186.63, "./working/income_normalized.csv"],\n      "balance_normalization": [0.0, 1999.0, "./working/balance_normalized.csv"]\n    },\n   