n- **High damage group**: 142 storms (after filtering missing duration)\n- **Low damage group**: 228 storms (after filtering missing duration)\n\n## Correlation Results\n\n| Group | Correlation (r) | p-value | Relationship Type |\n|-------|-----------------|---------|-------------------|\n| High Damage | 0.62 | 0.0000 | linear |\n| Low Damage | 0.64 | 0.0000 | linear |\n\n## Key Findings\n1. **Both groups show significant linear relationships** between maximum storm category and duration\n2. **High damage storms** (r=0.62) have a slightly weaker but still strong positive correlation\n3. **Low damage storms** (r=0.64) have a slightly stronger positive correlation\n4. **Both p-values are essentially 0**, indicating highly significant correlations (p < 0.05)\n5. **Both |r| values exceed 0.4**, confirming linear relationships for both groups\n\n## Interpretation\n- Higher storm categories tend to last longer for both high and low damage storms\n- The relationship is consistent across damage levels, suggesting storm intensity is a key factor in duration regardless of damage impact\n```\n```markdown\n{\n  "final_answer_block": {\n    "question_id": 431,\n    "answers": {\n      "high_damage_correlation_coefficient": 0.62,\n      "high_damage_p_value": 0.0,\n      "high_damage_relationship_type": "linear",\n      "low_damage_correlation_coefficient": 0.64,\n      "low_damage_p_value": 0.0,\n      "low_damage_relationship_type": "linear"\n    },\n    "format_targets": {\n      "high_damage_correlation_coefficient": "@high_damage_correlation_coefficient[0.62]",\n      "high_damage_p_value": "@high_damage_p_value[0.0]",\n      "high_damage_relationship_type": "@high_damage_relationship_type[linear]",\n      "low_damage_correlation_coefficient": "@low_damage_correlation_coefficient[0.64]",\n      "low_damage_p_value": "@low_damage_p_value[0.0]",\n      "low_damage_relationship_type": "@low_damage_relationship_type[linear]"\n    },\n    "evidence": {\n      "source_columns": ["