minimal independent path, explicitly satisfy every semantic oracle evidence field, reject narrow ML baselines, wrong ddof, and boundary mistakes before finalizing.\n\n```', 'response_content': '```markdown\n[STEP GOAL]: Load the abalone dataset and check for missing values in the required columns (Length, Diameter, Height, Whole weight, Shucked weight, Viscera weight, Shell weight)\n```\n```markdown\nI will start by loading the abalone dataset and examining the data structure. According to the Data Card, there are no missing values in any column, but I need to verify this and proceed with the preprocessing steps as specified.\n```\n```python\nimport pandas as pd\nimport numpy as np\nfrom sklearn.preprocessing import MinMaxScaler\nfrom scipy import stats\n\n# Load the abalone dataset\ndf = pd.read_csv(\'./input/abalone.csv\')\n\n# Display basic information about the dataset\nprint("Dataset shape:", df.shape)\nprint("\\nColumn names:", df.columns.tolist())\nprint("\\nMissing values per column:")\nprint(df.isnull().sum())\n```\n```markdown\nNow I need to select the required columns for preprocessing and perform the data preprocessing steps.\n```\n```python\n# Select the required columns for preprocessing\nrequired_columns = [\'Length\', \'Diameter\', \'Height\', \'Whole weight\', \'Shucked weight\', \'Viscera weight\', \'Shell weight\']\n\n# Check if all required columns exist\nmissing_columns = [col for col in required_columns if col not in df.columns]\nprint("Missing columns:", missing_columns if missing_columns else "None")\n\n# Extract the required columns\ndf_preprocess = df[required_columns].copy()\n\n# Check for missing values in the selected columns\nmissing_values_count = df_preprocess.isnull().sum().sum()\nprint(f"\\nTotal missing values in required columns: {missing_values_count}")\n```\n```markdown\nBased on the Data Card and the output, there are no missing values in the dataset. Now I will proceed with MinMaxScaler normalization and distribution analysis.\n```\n```python\n# Check if there are any missing values\nmissing_values_handled = "Yes" if missing_values_count == 0 else "No"\n\n# Apply MinMaxScaler to scale the variables to range 0-1\nscaler = MinMaxScaler(feature_range=(0, 1))\ndf_scaled = pd.DataFrame(scaler.fit_transform(df_preprocess), columns=required_columns)\n\n# Verify the range of scaled variables\nmin_values = df_scaled.min()\nmax_values = df_scaled.max()\nprint("Min values after scaling:", min_values.tolist())\nprint("Max values after scaling:", max_values.tolist())\n\n# Calculate skewness and kurtosis for distribution analysis\nskewness = df_scaled.skew()\nkurtosis = df_scaled.kurtosis()\n\nprint("\\nSkewness values:")\nprint(skewness)\nprint("\\nKurtosis values:")\nprint(kurtosis)\n```\n```markdown\nNow I need to determine the distribution type based on the skewness and kurtosis criteria:\n- If skewness is between -0.5 and 0.5 AND kurtosis is between -2 and 2, consider it as Normal\n- Otherwise, consider it as Non-Normal\n\nI\'ll check each column and determine the overall distribution type.\n```\n```python\n# Determine distribution type for each column\ndistribution_results = {}\nfor col in required_columns:\n    skew = skewness[col]\n    kurt = kurtosis[col]\n    is_normal = (-0.5 <= skew <= 0.5) and (-2 <= kurt <= 2)\n    distribution_results[col] = "Normal" if is_normal else "Non-Normal"\n\nprint("Distribution type for each column:")\nfor col, dist_type in distribution_results.items():\n    print(f"{col}: {dist_type} (skewness={skewness[col]:.4f}, kurtosis={kurtosis[col]:.4f})")\n\n# Determine overall distribution type (if all columns are Normal, then overall is Normal)\nall_normal = all(dist_type == "Normal" for dist_type in distribution_results.values())\noverall_distribution_type = "Normal" if all_normal else "Non-Normal"\n\nprint(f"\\nOverall distribution type: {overall_distribution_type}")\n```\n```markdown\nNow I have all the information needed to create the final answer block. Let me verify the results and create the FinalAnswerBlock.\n```\n```python\n# Verify the results\nprint("=== Final Results ===")\nprint(f"Missing values handled: {missing_values_handled}")\nprint(f"Min-Max scaler scale range: 0-1")\nprint(f"Overall distribution type: {overall_distribution_type}")\n\n# Create the final answer block\nfinal_answer_block = {\n    "final_answer_block": {\n        "question_id": 550,\n        "answers": {\n            "missing_values_handled": missing_values_handled,\n            "min_max_scaler_scale": "0-1",\n            "distribution_type": overall_distribution_type\n        },\n        "format_targets": {\n            "missing_values_handled": "@missing_values_handled[Yes]",\n            "min_max_scaler_scale": "@min_max_scaler_scale[0-1]",\n            "distribution_type": f"@distribution_type[{overall_distribution_type}]"\n        },\n        "evidence": {\n            "source_columns": required_columns,\n            "sample_size": len(df),\n            "method": "MinMaxScaler normalization with skewness and kurtosis distribution analysis",\n            "oracle_evidence": {\n                "missing_values_count": int(missing_values_count),\n                "scaled_range_min": float(min_values.min()),\n                "scaled_range_max": float(max_values.max())\n            }\n        },\n        "verified": True,\n        "validator_report_id": None\n    }\n}\n\nprint("\\nFinal Answer Block:")\nimport json\nprint(json.dumps(final_answer_block, indent=2))\n```\n```markdown\n[STEP GOAL]: Complete the task by displaying the FinalAnswerBlock in the required format\n```\n```markdown\nThe task is complete. I have:\n1. Loaded the abalone dataset and verified there are no missing values\n2. Applied MinMaxScaler to scale the required columns to range 0-1\n3. Performed distribution analysis using skewness and kurtosis\n4. Determined the overall distribution type based on the criteria\n\nThe final answer block has been created with all required fields